---
version: 33.1.0
date: February 12th, 2025
---

![What's New in AG Grid 33.1](/whats-new/whats-new-33-1.png)

AG Grid Enterprise 33.1 is an important release that improves stability, reduces bundle size, speeds up scrolling, and enhances accessibility.

Key additions in this release:

1. [Row Numbers](#row-numbers)
2. [Row Spanning](#row-spanning)
3. [Tree Data Nested Records](#tree-data-nested-records)
4. [Master/Detail Tri-State Checkbox Selection](#masterdetail-tri-state-checkbox-selection)
5. [Accessibility Improvements](#accessibility-improvements)

Please note that AG Grid 33.1 has no breaking changes from AG Grid 33.0. If you're already using AG Grid 33.0, this upgrade doesn't require any changes to your codebase.

We recommend reviewing the migration guide when planning to update to this version.

## Row Numbers

AG Grid 33.1 allows showing a row numbers column, similar to Excel. If cell selection is enabled, clicking or dragging over the row number cell selects all the cells of the row. This enables users to easily identify rows and quickly select ranges of entire rows directly without having to go from the first to the last cell in the selected row range.

{% video videoSrc="/whats-new/ag-grid-33.2-row-span-pagination-demo.mp4" isPublic=true /%}

## Row Spanning

AG Grid 33.1 adds row spanning, which automatically merges identical cell values across rows. This enables the grid to display a more sparse view of the data and allows users to more easily spot rows with identical cell values in a column.

{% video videoSrc="/whats-new/ag-grid-33-1-row-spanning-demo.mp4" isPublic=true /%}

## Master/Detail Tri-State Checkbox Selection

AG Grid 33.1 adds master/detail tri-state checkbox selection from master to detail rows. This enables users to select master/detail rows according to the hierarchical data structure to quickly process the rows they want.

{% video videoSrc="/ag-grid-33-1-master-detail-tri-state.mp4" isPublic=true /%}

## Tree Data Nested Records

AG Grid 33.1 enables tree data to display hierarchical self-referencing data where the children are provided as an array in each node. This new feature avoids the need to transform the data before it's provided to the grid and enables users to interact with this type of hierarchical data using the standard feature set in AG Grid.

## Accessibility Improvements

AG Grid 33.1 improves accessibility support across menus by providing detailed ARIA labeling for screen readers and improving the keyboard navigation experience. This is part of our ongoing work on accessibility support and enables the grid to generate appropriate announcements for screen readers and deliver more intuitive and comprehensive keyboard navigation.

## Summary

AG Grid 33.1 is a key minor version—it reduces bundle size and adds important end-user features as well as improvements in performance and quality. We suggest reviewing the migration guide when planning to upgrade and seeing the full list of changes in our changelog.